# Terminal Command Execution

Avoid using `cd` in commands. Execute directly using the complete absolute path.

## ❌ Avoid

```bash
cd c:\Users\marco\Desktop\Projects\Iberus\subdir
npm install
```

```powershell
cd project\build
cmake ..
```

## ✅ Prefer

Run commands with full paths. Use the `working_directory` parameter when needed, or pass absolute paths in the command:

```powershell
npm install
```
(with `working_directory: c:\Users\marco\Desktop\Projects\Iberus\subdir`)

```powershell
cmake c:\Users\marco\Desktop\Projects\Iberus\project\build ..
```

Do not chain `cd` with other commands; execute directly with complete paths.
